WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:04.260
Unit eight. Supporting Someone in Crisis!

2
00:00:05.210 --> 00:00:09.987
Hello, everyone! I'm Doctor Sokha, your school doctor.

3
00:00:10.037 --> 00:00:13.082
Hi, Doctor Sokha! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:13.133 --> 00:00:17.988
Today we learn about Supporting Someone in Crisis. Let's go!

5
00:00:19.141 --> 00:00:23.258
Crisis. Say it with me. Crisis!

6
00:00:26.774 --> 00:00:30.341
Listen. Say it with me. Listen!

7
00:00:33.837 --> 00:00:37.254
Stay. Say it with me. Stay!

8
00:00:40.771 --> 00:00:44.738
Safety. Say it with me. Safety!

9
00:00:48.276 --> 00:00:52.709
Emergency. Say it with me. Emergency!

10
00:00:56.189 --> 00:01:00.389
Trusted adult. Say it with me. Trusted adult!

11
00:01:03.861 --> 00:01:08.244
Professional help. Say it with me. Professional help!

12
00:01:11.749 --> 00:01:16.833
Self-care. Say it with me. Self-care!

13
00:01:20.395 --> 00:01:35.444
If someone is in crisis, listen calmly and stay with them. If there is any risk to their safety, contact a trusted adult, professional help, or emergency services immediately. Supporting others also requires self-care.

14
00:01:35.494 --> 00:01:38.902
Now I understand. Thank you, Doctor Sokha!

15
00:01:39.762 --> 00:01:44.923
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:44.973 --> 00:01:46.123
Stay!

17
00:01:47.171 --> 00:01:52.359
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:52.409 --> 00:01:53.922
Professional help!

19
00:01:54.876 --> 00:02:03.147
Did you know? Asking someone directly how they are feeling does not put ideas in their head — it can open the door to help!

20
00:02:03.197 --> 00:02:05.485
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:02:06.540 --> 00:02:15.091
Think and answer. Who could you contact if a friend is in crisis?

22
00:02:15.141 --> 00:02:16.291
Great answer!

23
00:02:17.318 --> 00:02:23.182
Great job today! Stay healthy, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
00:02:23.232 --> 00:02:26.000
Goodbye, everyone! Stay healthy!

